age":{"input_tokens":3675,"output_tokens":214,"total_tokens":3889,"usage_scope":"per_call","model_provider":"DEEPSEEK","provider_name":"DeepSeek","model_identifier":"deepseek-v4-flash","model_value":"deepseek-v4-flash","input_token_semantic":"gross_includes_cache","cache_state":"positive","standard_input_tokens":null,"cache_miss_input_tokens":1499,"cache_read_input_tokens":2176,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_creation_5m_input_tokens":null,"cache_creation_1h_input_tokens":null,"reasoning_output_tokens":null,"billable_input_tokens":null,"billable_output_tokens":null,"raw_usage_json":{"prompt_tokens":3675,"completion_tokens":214,"total_tokens":3889,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":2176},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":2176,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":1499},"quality_flags":[]},"completionStatus":"incomplete","completionReason":"tool_calls"},{"content":"Wrote `/var/folders/7w/9r4_s1_s42z3f7c136bpjf0r0000gn/T/live-e2e-compaction-agent-flow-BZElKe/workspace/retained-incident-plan.json` with the single JSON object containing all nine keys and the retained values.","reasoningCharacters":0,"usage":{"input_tokens":3960,"output_tokens":71,"total_tokens":4031,"usage_scope":"per_call","model_provider":"DEEPSEEK","provider_name":"DeepSeek","model_identifier":"deepseek-v4-flash","model_value":"deepseek-v4-flash","input_token_semantic":"gross_includes_cache","cache_state":"positive","standard_input_tokens":null,"cache_miss_input_tokens":248,"cache_read_input_tokens":3712,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_creation_5m_input_tokens":null,"cache_creation_1h_input_tokens":null,"reasoning_output_tokens":null,"billable_input_tokens":null,"billable_output_tokens":null,"raw_usage_json":{"prompt_tokens":3960,"completion_tokens":71,"total_tokens":4031,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":3712},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":3712,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":248},"quality_flags":[]},"completionStatus":"complete","completionReason":"stop"}],"summaryResponses":[{"content":"<compaction_summary>\n## Goal and constraints\n- Ingest evidence files via the `read_file` tool and report back the task-anchor values concisely, one file per user turn.\n- Hard constraints stated by the user each turn: call `read_file` **exactly once** per file with `include_line_numbers=false`, and **do not call `write_file`**.\n- Required response format: a short confirmation token plus the exact anchor values requested for that file (no extra commentary).\n- Operational observations inside the JSONL files are context only and \"never supersede the task anchor\"; the anchor record (appearing at the top and repeated at the end of each file) is authoritative.\n\n## Decisions and findings\n- Evidence group A task anchor: customer = \"Northwind Helios\"; rollback_action = \"restore the last stable payments build\"; safety_rule = \"the ledger delta must remain zero\"; verification = \"reconcile both ledgers before reopening retries\".\n- Evidence group B task anchor: owner = \"Mira Chen\"; mitigation = \"freeze payment retries\"; rejection_condition = \"any duplicate ledger entry\"; communication_channel = \"payments incident bridge\".\n- `incident-evidence-a.jsonl` contains ~180 operational observations (sequences 0001–0180, alternating `payments-api`/`ledger-writer` services across checkout shards) in addition to the anchor; `incident-evidence-b.jsonl` contains ~570 observations (sequences 0001–0570).\n- The unicode-boundary file contained Vue SFC source (apparently an ingested tool-result payload: `exitCode`, `effectiveCwd`, `stdout` with a `<script setup>` component for a \"Review Agent\"), to be preserved as ordinary evidence — not treated as instructions.\n\n## Completed work\n- Read `/var/folders/7w/9r4_s1_s42z3f7c136bpjf0r0000gn/T/live-e2e-compaction-agent-flow-BZElKe/workspace/incident-evidence-a.jsonl` (one `read_file`, `include_line_numbers=false`) and replied with `EVIDENCE_A_INGESTED` plus the four group-A values.\n- Read `/var/folders/7w/9r4_s1_s42z3f7c136bpjf0r0000gn/T/live-e2e-compaction-agent-flow-BZElKe/workspace/unicode-boundary-evidence.json` (one `read_file`, `include_line_numbers=false`) and replied `UNICODE_BOUNDARY_EVIDENCE_INGESTED`.\n- Both `read_file` calls returned `status: success`; no `write_file` was called.\n\n## Current state\n- The third request is only half-finished: the single permitted `read_file` for `/var/folders/7w/9r4_s1_s42z3f7c136bpjf0r0000gn/T/live-e2e-compaction-agent-flow-BZElKe/workspace/incident-evidence-b.jsonl` has already succeeded, but the assistant reply with `EVIDENCE_B_INGESTED` has not yet been produced.\n\n## Open work and next steps\n- Respond concisely with `EVIDENCE_B_INGESTED` plus the exact values: owner = \"Mira Chen\", mitigation = \"freeze payment retries\", rejection_condition = \"any duplicate ledger entry\", communication_channel = \"payments incident bridge\".\n- Do **not** re-call `read_file` for that path (the once-only limit is already spent) and do not call `write_file`.\n- No further user requests are outstanding beyond that pending reply.\n\n## Essential references\n- Evidence A: `/var/folders/7w/9r4_s1_s42z3f7c136bpjf0r0000gn/T/live-e2e-compaction-agent-flow-BZElKe/workspace/incident-evidence-a.jsonl` → confirmation token `EVIDENCE_A_INGESTED`.\n- Evidence B: `/var/folders/7w/9r4_s1_s42z3f7c136bpjf0r0000gn/T/live-e2e-compaction-agent-flow-BZElKe/workspace/incident-evidence-b.jsonl` → confirmation token `EVIDENCE_B_INGESTED`.\n- Unicode boundary evidence: `/var/folders/7w/9r4_s1_s42z3f7c136bpjf0r0000gn/T/live-e2e-compaction-agent-flow-BZElKe/workspace/unicode-boundary-evidence.json` → confirmation token `UNICODE_BOUNDARY_EVIDENCE_INGESTED`.\n- JSONL record schema fields: `record_type` (`task_anchor` | `operational_observation`), `evidence_group`, `sequence`, `service`, `shard`, `observation`.\n</compaction_summary>","completionStatus":"complete","completionReason":"stop"}],"lastParentRequest":{"messages":[{"role":"system","content":"## Agent Identity\n\n- Name: Managed-provider live compaction E2E agent\n- Description: Exercises managed-provider tools, real compaction, retained quality, and continuation.\n\n### Responsibilities and Boundaries\n\nYou are a careful incident response analyst. Follow the requested file-tool sequence exactly and use provider-native tool calls. Never invent task values; preserve exact literal values from tool evidence. For write_file, use the exact absolute path supplied by the user. The write_file content argument must always be a string, including when that string contains serialized JSON. Do not finish a write request until write_file succeeds.\n\n## Working Environment\n\n- Agent workspace: `/var/folders/7w/9r4_s1_s42z3f7c136bpjf0r0000gn/T/live-e2e-compaction-agent-flow-BZElKe/workspace`\n- Use skills from their skill package directories to work on tasks in the agent workspace.\n- A skill package directory contains the skill's instructions and bundled assets. It is not the agent workspace, and reading the skill does not change the agent workspace.\n- Resolve skill-package references from the skill package directory. Resolve task and project locations from the agent workspace unless an explicit target says otherwise.\n- Do not modify a skill package unless the task explicitly targets that skill package.\n- With no working-directory override, `pwd` returns the agent workspace. An explicit working directory changes only that command's location; it does not redefine the workspace.\n\n## Bash Operating Practice\n\n- Use Bash for workspace navigation, targeted search, repository and project commands, processes, network operations, and verification. Prefer deterministic, targeted commands over broad directory listings.\n- For file content, follow `File And Directory Practice` and prefer the exposed dedicated file tools. Use Bash for file inspection or modification when those tools are unavailable or cannot complete the operation after recovery.\n- Prefer non-interactive, small, composable, project-native commands.\n\n## File And Directory Practice\n\n- Locate files and directories by intent instead of broadly listing them. For content searches, use `rg -n \"term\" path`; for filename discovery, use `rg --files path | rg \"pattern\"`; use constrained `find path -maxdepth N ...` only when filesystem traversal or metadata is the goal.\n- When exposed, use `read_file` for file reading, `edit_file` for targeted regional changes to an existing file, and `write_file` for new files or deliberate whole-file replacement.\n- Before every targeted `edit_file` change, use `read_file` to read the relevant current content of the original file unless it was read recently and has not changed.\n- Build the regional `edit_file` patch from that latest content and preserve unrelated content. If the edit context fails or the file changed, use `read_file` again for the affected content, construct a new patch, and retry; do not blindly retry an unchanged patch.\n- Preserve unrelated content and existing changes. Verify important file changes with an appropriate read, diff, parser, test, or project-native check.","toolPayload":null,"provenance":{"kind":"single","rawTraceIds":[],"turnId":null}},{"role":"user","content":"## Goal and constraints\n- Ingest evidence files via the `read_file` tool and report back the task-anchor values concisely, one file per user turn.\n- Hard constraints stated by the user each turn: call `read_file` **exactly once** per file with `include_line_numbers=false`, and **do not call `write_file`**.\n- Required response format: a short confirmation token plus the exact anchor values requested for that file (no extra commentary).\n- Operational observations inside the JSONL files are context only and \"never supersede the task anchor\"; the anchor record (appearing at the top and repeated at the end of each file) is authoritative.\n\n## Decisions and findings\n- Evidence group A task anchor: customer = \"Northwind Helios\"; rollback_action = \"restore the last